[CHANGE] benchmark_4/parts/inter_interface/pretense/inter_interface_impl_pretense.py: Resolved the deterministic-scenario coverage feedback for Allocator: the impl pseudo-state machine now mirrors the contracted failure branches (non-positive allocate/release amounts -> AllocationLimitError; allocate beyond vault reserves -> InsufficientFundsError) around the call_target pivot, and TestInterInterfaceImplReal adds deterministic scenarios for allocate(0)/(-5), release(0)/(1), and allocate(INITIAL_VAULT_RESERVES+1) beyond the provisioned collaborator vault. The fuzz fixture provisions exactly INITIAL_VAULT_RESERVES so the real vault balance tracks the model's mirrored reserves, keeping the insufficient-reserve branch matched between model and SUT instead of raising unexpected errors.
[CHANGE] benchmark_4/parts/inter_interface/pretense/vault_impl_pretense.py: Resolved overspecified-oracle feedback: removed the duplicated withdrawal/deposit rejection guards from the implementation pseudo-state machine. The impl overrides now only observe the real SUT around the call_target pivot (balance delta asserts) and no longer re-evaluate model precondition branches against post-mutation self.state, which previously turned a valid withdraw(1) after deposit(1) into a spurious expected InsufficientFundsError. Contracted failure outcomes (invalid amounts, inactive vault) remain declared once by the inherited interface transitions, and the deterministic rejection scenarios in TestVaultImplReal are retained.
